IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Papua New Guinea (Members of the Forces Benefits) Act 1957 (Cth). Source:
-- ../registers/source-bundle/C1957A00089.txt. Seat: the member or dependant.

§ `Nouns`

DECLARE `Service record` HAS
    -- s 3
    `a male indigenous inhabitant of PNG or a Pacific island` IS A BOOLEAN
    `served in the Defence Force from`                  IS A DATE
    `paid below the minimum AMF male rate`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `service ended by discharge or death`               IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 5(1)-(2)
    `occurrence during war service`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `arose out of or attributable to service`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `pre-existing cause aggravated by service conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 5(3)
    `serious default or wilful act`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `intentionally self-inflicted`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `serious breach of discipline`                      IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Forces position` HAS
    `a member of the Forces`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commonwealth is liable for incapacity or death` IS A BOOLEAN
    `benefits are limited to this Act and the War Gratuity Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `pension is inalienable`                            IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Rules`

-- s 3: "served during the war" — the war from 3 September 1939, including
-- wars entered before 3 September 1945. Service that began before the war is
-- taken to have continued into it (F1, changed after the independent pass).
@ref s 3
GIVEN s IS A `Service record`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a member of the Forces under s 3` s IF
        s's `a male indigenous inhabitant of PNG or a Pacific island`
    AND s's `served in the Defence Force from` LESS THAN Date 3 9 1945
    AND s's `paid below the minimum AMF male rate`
    AND s's `service ended by discharge or death`

-- s 5
@ref s 5
GIVEN s IS A `Service record`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Commonwealth is liable under s 5` s IF
        `a member of the Forces under s 3` s
    AND (s's `occurrence during war service` OR s's `arose out of or attributable to service` OR s's `pre-existing cause aggravated by service conditions`)
    AND NOT (s's `serious default or wilful act` OR s's `intentionally self-inflicted` OR s's `serious breach of discipline`)

@ref ss 3-6, 8
@export default The position of a member of the Forces (or dependant) under the Papua New Guinea (Members of the Forces Benefits) Act 1957 (Cth): whether the person is a member of the Forces (s 3), whether the Commonwealth is liable to pay pension or compensation for incapacity or death connected with war service (s 5, at rates in the regulations), that the benefits are only those under this Act and the War Gratuity Act (s 4), and that a pension is inalienable (s 8). DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN s IS A `Service record`  @desc The service record and the circumstances of the incapacity or death
GIVETH A `Forces position`
`the forces position for` s MEANS
    `Forces position` WITH
        `a member of the Forces`                        IS `a member of the Forces under s 3` s
        `the Commonwealth is liable for incapacity or death` IS `the Commonwealth is liable under s 5` s
        `benefits are limited to this Act and the War Gratuity Act` IS `a member of the Forces under s 3` s
        `pension is inalienable`                        IS `a member of the Forces under s 3` s
